<title>UK: Kingfisher, Dixons up on &quot;windfall&quot; hopes.</title>
<headline>Kingfisher, Dixons up on &quot;windfall&quot; hopes.</headline>
<dateline>LONDON 1997-07-15</dateline>
<text>
<p>Shares in Kingfisher Plc  and electronic goods retailer Dixons Group Plc rose following upbeat comments from the British Retail Consortium (BRC).</p>
<p>The BRC said &quot;windfall&quot; cash from building society flotations was filtering into &quot;big ticket&quot; purchases such as electrical goods, furniture and kitchen appliances.</p>
<p>Kingfisher owns electrical stores chain Comet.</p>
<p>-- London newsroom +44 171 542 7717</p>
